Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Summer kiosk -- grant the microphone to summer-ttu.onrender.com in Microsoft Edge,
; silently and permanently, so the wall's wake word works after an unattended 7am boot
; with NO "Allow microphone?" prompt. This is a machine-wide Edge policy.
;
; HOW TO USE:
;   1. Double-click this file on the ThinkCentre.
;   2. Accept the UAC prompt and the "add to registry?" prompt (needs admin rights).
;   3. Fully close Edge and reopen it (or just reboot).
;   4. Verify: open Edge, go to  edge://policy  -- you should see
;      "AudioCaptureAllowedUrls" listed with the Summer URL.
;
; Also make sure Windows itself allows it (one-time, separate from this file):
;   Settings > Privacy & security > Microphone > turn ON "Microphone access",
;   "Let apps access your microphone", and "Let desktop apps access your microphone".
;
; This grants ONLY the microphone, and ONLY to Summer's site (least privilege) --
; not the camera, and no other website.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge\AudioCaptureAllowedUrls]
"1"="https://summer-ttu.onrender.com"
